VLA Forge

Third-party material and design credits.

1. SO-101 robot model (vendor/so101)
   From TheRobotStudio's SO-ARM100 repository, https://github.com/TheRobotStudio/SO-ARM100
   Licensed under the Apache License 2.0. MJCF and STL meshes are used unmodified.

2. Wood texture (web/assets/wood_diff.jpg, wood_rough.jpg)
   "Wood Table 001" from Poly Haven, https://polyhaven.com, CC0.

3. three.js (web/vendor/three)
   https://threejs.org, MIT License.

4. Interface design
   The editor layout and visual language of the page (top bar with segmented tabs, chat panel with tool
   status pills, floating tool groups on the canvas, bottom tab bar and the Geist / Geist Mono
   type set, two of the families heypcb.ai loads) are modelled on the public website of HeyPCB, https://heypcb.ai.
   HeyPCB's open-source repositories (github.com/heypcb) contain hardware designs under CERN-OHL-S and an
   MIT-licensed MCP server, but no interface code, so nothing was copied: the look was recreated from the
   public site with this project's own HTML, CSS and JavaScript. No HeyPCB logo, name or asset appears in
   the interface. HeyPCB is not affiliated with this project.

4a. Motion and mascot
   The animations (entrance rises, keycap buttons with a halo ring, blink, float, cheer, ripple, thought
   cloud, shimmer loaders) are ported from Etch, the author's own earlier project, and recoloured to this
   page's factory safety-orange accent (#ff5a1f). The robot mascot is an original character, built from square
   tiles and drawn in code (web/mascot.js): hazard-stripe hard hat, dark visor, two tall pixel eyes, no mouth,
   in the spirit of simple chatbot icons; it is not a copy of any company's mark.

5. Fonts
   Geist and Geist Mono (Vercel, SIL Open Font License 1.1), loaded from Google Fonts. No other typeface.

6. Encoders
   facebook/dinov2-small (Apache-2.0) and google/siglip2-base-patch16-224 (Apache-2.0), loaded from the
   local Hugging Face cache.

7. Robot parts for the builder (vendor/menagerie)
   From MuJoCo Menagerie, https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco_menagerie, commit
   98a70c569c4c1b6da467a20012f766ee1f8dc521, used unmodified, each folder with its upstream LICENSE:
   trs_so_arm100 (Apache-2.0), low_cost_robot_arm (Apache-2.0), trossen_wx250s and trossen_vx300s
   (BSD-3-Clause, Trossen Robotics), robotiq_2f85 (BSD-2-Clause, ROS-Industrial), franka_emika_panda hand.xml
   (Apache-2.0). Full table in SOURCES.md.

8. Factory line tote (vendor/robosuite)
   bins_arena.xml from robosuite, https://github.com/ARISE-Initiative/robosuite, commit
   5ce6643f3092639d08f7b0f90ed1c6a84f50552c, MIT License (Copyright (c) 2022 Stanford Vision and Learning Lab
   and UT Robot Perception and Learning Lab), kept unmodified with its LICENSE; bin1's collision boxes are
   scaled at run time (src/vla_forge/sim/line.py). The conveyor follows the construction given by MuJoCo's
   maintainers in google-deepmind/mujoco issue #547. Details in SOURCES.md.
